  "text": "ooooh, that looks close, and Marais Erasmus has a loooong think before raising his finger. Bairstow has reviewed it. Reverse-sweeps from a ball pitching in line with the stumps, but is it turning down the leg side, maybe? Nope. It's pitching just inside the line of leg stump, and it's only turned enough from there to straighten and hit the inside half of leg stump, according to ball-tracking. England are six down",
